        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(exec): validate script files outside the workspace root for shell bleed",
        "body": "> [!NOTE]\n> **AI-Assisted Contribution:** This PR was prepared and validated with the assistance of an AI coding assistant (Antigravity/Gemini).\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where script preflight shell bleed variable injection bypass (pr #100860).\n\n**Symptom/Behavior:**\nIf `resolvePreflightRelativePath` returns `null` (which happens when the path starts with `..` or is an absolute path outside the workspace root), the loop executes `if (!relativePath) continue;`, silently skipping validation. This allows unvalidated scripts located outside the workspace directory to bypass safety controls.\n\nAffected location: `[src/agents/bash-tools.exec.ts](file://src/agents/bash-tools.exec.ts#L1202-L1208) (compiled as `dist/bash-tools-CMeLXzt9.js`)`\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nImplemented a surgical fix to resolve the logic discrepancy.\n\n**Solution Overview:**\nBlock execution of unvalidated scripts outside the workspace, or validate them using absolute paths:\n  ```javascript\n  const relativePath = resolvePreflightRelativePath({\n      rootDir: params.workdir,\n      absPath\n  });\n  if (!relativePath) {\n      throw new Error(`exec preflight: script ${path.basename(absPath)} is outside the workspace root and cannot be safely validated.`);\n  }\n  ```\n\n## User Impact\n\nCorrects behavior to ensure that: Any executed script parsed by the interpreter preflight check should be validated for shell bleed variable injections. If a script path is outside the workspace root, it should either be resolved via its absolute path and validated, or blocked from executing.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Unit Tests / Verification Suite\n- Unit tests in `src/agents/bash-tools.exec.script-preflight.test.ts` run and pass successfully.\n\n### Real Behavior Proof\n\n#### Outside Workspace Script Preflight Verification:\nWe executed a verification script targeting a file located outside the workspace root that contains shell bleed variable injections. The output shows that the preflight engine successfully intercepts it and throws the correct injection error instead of bypassing it:\n\n```text\n[VERIFICATION] Preflight validation for outside script:\n  Workspace Directory: /tmp/openclaw-verify-preflight-DUS7B4/workspace\n  Outside Script Path: /tmp/openclaw-verify-preflight-DUS7B4/outside-injected.js\n\n[SUCCESS] Caught preflight error as expected: exec preflight: detected likely shell variable injection ($DM_JSON) in node script: outside-injected.js:1.\nIn Node.js, use process.env[\"DM_JSON\"] instead of raw $DM_JSON.\n(If this is inside a string literal on purpose, escape it or restructure the code.)\n\n[SUCCESS] Script preflight outside workspace root is correctly validated!\n```\n\n#### After (Passing Verification):\n```text\nScope: all 159 workspace projects\nLockfile is up to date, resolution step is skipped\nProgress: resolved 0, reused 1, downloaded 0, added 0\nPackages: +1 -173\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProgress: resolved 0, reused 174, downloaded 0, added 1, done\n\n. preinstall$ node scripts/preinstall-package-manager-warning.mjs\n. preinstall: Done\n. postinstall$ node scripts/postinstall-bundled-plugins.mjs\n. postinstall: Done\n. prepare$ node scripts/prepare-git-hooks.mjs\n. prepare: Done\nDone in 2.6s using pnpm v11.2.2\n\n RUN  v4.1.9 /home/dietpi/Developer/openclaw\n\n ✓ |agents| src/agents/bash-tools.exec.script-preflight.test.ts (61 tests | 4 skipped) 348ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  57 passed | 4 skipped (61)\n   Start at  12:39:44\n   Duration  3.95s (transform 2.17s, setup 120ms, import 3.36s, tests 348ms, environment 0ms)\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/4.1-script-preflight-outside-workspace-validation",
